Alex,

Here is a reduced example with the error I´m getting:

First the Java Interface:
package rb.scicom;

public interface BogusInterface {

    public Object run(Object... objs);
}

Now the Ruby code:
  # Create a class that implements the Java BogusInterface
  class Bogus
    include Java::RbScicom.BogusInterface

    attr_reader :ruby_obj

    def initialize(ruby_obj)
      @ruby_obj = ruby_obj
    end

    # Method run with two arguments: the method name and a varargs
    def run(method, *args)
      @ruby_obj.send(method, *args)
    end

  end

  # Create a Matrix in Ruby
  props1 = [1, 2, 3]

  # Pack the matrix in a Bogus class
  cb = Bogus.new(props1)

  # Assign the cb variable to an x variable in R
  R.assign("x", cb)

  # Call method 'run' giving it the 'length' method name
  R.eval("x$run('length')")

This returns:
"Cannot match arguments (character) to any JVM method overload:\n\n\tpublic java.lang.Object
SciComTest$$Bogus_359443912.run(java.lang.Object[])"

